1:["$","$Ld",null,{"page":{"id":"library--freeflow-immersion","kind":"library-article","route":"/roadmap/library/freeflow-immersion","sourceUrl":"https://refold.la/roadmap/library/freeflow-immersion","sourceHash":"bea3a8a1b402d8335c39600e1faf319720b3427d1a46073be44ff461af8fb2a1","collectedAt":"2026-09-01T16:52:57.281Z","bodyMode":"authorized-full-body","title":{"en":"Freeflow Immersion","zh":"自由流沉浸"},"description":{"en":"","zh":""},"segments":[{"id":"segment-0001","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Freeflow immersion is any time you engage with content in the target language without stopping, looking things up, or actively trying to decode. You just let the language flow over you and focus on the content — the story, the conversation, the information.","zh":"自由流沉浸是指接触目标语言内容时，不暂停、不查资料，也不主动尝试逐一解码。你只需让语言自然地流过，专注于内容本身——故事、对话或信息。"}},{"id":"segment-0002","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Want to see some examples of Freeflow activities? <a href=\"https://refold.la/learning-libraries?libraryType=activities&amp;pillar=Freeflow\">-&gt; Freeflow Activities</a>","zh":"想看看自由流活动的示例吗？<a href=\"https://refold.la/learning-libraries?libraryType=activities&amp;pillar=Freeflow\">-&gt; 自由流活动</a>"}},{"id":"how-it-works","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"How It Works","zh":"运作方式"}},{"id":"segment-0004","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"During freeflow, you accept whatever you understand and let go of what you don't. No pausing, no dictionary, no replaying. If you miss a word, you keep going. If you lose the thread, you try to pick it back up from context. The goal is to process the language at natural speed.","zh":"进行自由流沉浸时，理解多少就接受多少，不理解的部分就先放下。不暂停、不查词典、不重播。如果漏掉一个词，就继续。如果跟丢了内容脉络，就尝试根据上下文重新跟上。目标是以自然语速处理语言。"}},{"id":"segment-0005","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"This is fundamentally different from interactive immersion, where you're actively working to understand every sentence. Both are important, but they train different things. Interactive builds knowledge; freeflow builds automaticity and speed.","zh":"这与互动式沉浸有本质区别；在互动式沉浸中，你会主动努力理解每一个句子。两者都很重要，但训练的能力不同。互动式沉浸帮助你积累知识；自由流沉浸则培养自动化处理能力和速度。"}},{"id":"why-it-matters","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"Why It Matters","zh":"为什么重要"}},{"id":"segment-0007","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Your brain needs practice processing language in real-time. All the vocabulary and grammar you've learned through priming and interactive immersion lives in your conscious knowledge — you can access it if you pause and think. Freeflow trains your brain to access that knowledge automatically, without pausing.","zh":"你的大脑需要练习实时处理语言。你通过预激和互动式沉浸学到的词汇与语法，都存在于你的显性知识中——只要停下来思考，你就能调用它们。自由流沉浸训练大脑自动调用这些知识，无须停顿。"}},{"id":"segment-0008","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Freeflow also builds stamina. Extended periods of target-language engagement — watching a full movie, reading a whole chapter, listening to a long podcast — are how you train your brain to sustain focus in the language.","zh":"自由流沉浸还能增强耐力。长时间接触目标语言——看完一整部电影、读完一整章、听一期很长的播客——能够训练大脑在使用这门语言时持续保持专注。"}},{"id":"when-to-start","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"When to Start","zh":"何时开始"}},{"id":"segment-0010","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Freeflow is introduced in Phase 1D and grows steadily from there. At first, it's best done with familiar content: things you've already gone through interactively, dubbed versions of media you know, or content well below your current level. As your comprehension improves, you can freeflow with increasingly difficult and unfamiliar content.","zh":"自由流沉浸会在第 1D 阶段引入，此后所占比重会稳步增加。刚开始时，最好选择熟悉的内容：你已经以互动方式学过的材料、你熟悉的影视作品的目标语言配音版，或明显低于你当前水平的内容。随着理解能力提高，你可以逐渐用难度更高、更陌生的内容进行自由流沉浸。"}},{"id":"what-counts-as-freeflow","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"What Counts as Freeflow","zh":"哪些活动算自由流沉浸"}},{"id":"segment-0012","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Anything where you're engaging with the language without tools or pausing:","zh":"任何不借助工具、不暂停，直接接触这门语言的活动都算："}},{"id":"segment-0013","type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"en":"Watching TV without subtitles (or with TL subtitles but no pausing)","zh":"不看字幕观看电视节目（或者使用目标语言字幕，但不暂停）"},{"en":"Listening to podcasts or audiobooks","zh":"收听播客或有声书"},{"en":"Reading books, articles, social media without a dictionary","zh":"不查词典，直接阅读书籍、文章和社交媒体内容"},{"en":"Rewatching content you've already studied interactively","zh":"重新观看你已经以互动方式学习过的内容"},{"en":"Background listening (lower value, but still useful)","zh":"背景听力（价值较低，但仍有帮助）"}]},{"id":"segment-0014","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"<a href=\"https://refold.la/learning-libraries?libraryType=activities&amp;pillar=Freeflow\">-&gt; Freeflow Activities</a>","zh":"<a href=\"https://refold.la/learning-libraries?libraryType=activities&amp;pillar=Freeflow\">-&gt; 自由流活动</a>"}},{"id":"tips","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"Tips","zh":"建议"}},{"id":"segment-0016","type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"en":"If you understand very little, you're not ready for freeflow with that content. Use easier or more familiar material.","zh":"如果你几乎听不懂或看不懂，就说明你还没准备好用这份内容进行自由流沉浸。请改用更简单或更熟悉的材料。"},{"en":"Freeflow should feel enjoyable, not torturous. If it's miserable, either the content is too hard or you need more interactive time first.","zh":"自由流沉浸应该让人觉得愉快，而不是备受折磨。如果过程很痛苦，要么是内容太难，要么是你需要先增加互动式沉浸的时间。"},{"en":"The Multipass Method works well with freeflow: go through content interactively first, then freeflow it afterward.","zh":"多遍学习法很适合与自由流沉浸结合：先以互动方式学习内容，之后再用同一内容进行自由流沉浸。"},{"en":"Don't count passive background noise as quality freeflow time. You need to be focused on understanding.","zh":"不要把被动的背景噪声算作高质量的自由流沉浸时间。你需要专注于理解内容。"}]},{"id":"research-and-reasoning","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"Research and Reasoning","zh":"研究与原理"}},{"id":"segment-0018","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Freeflow immersion is grounded in skill acquisition theory (DeKeyser, 2014), which describes how abilities move from controlled processing (conscious, effortful, slow) to automatic processing (unconscious, effortless, fast). Initial language learning involves a lot of controlled processing — looking words up, thinking about grammar rules, translating. Fluency requires converting this knowledge to automatic processing, which happens only through repeated, sustained exposure without conscious analysis.","zh":"自由流沉浸以技能习得理论（DeKeyser，2014）为基础。该理论描述了能力如何从受控处理（有意识、费力、缓慢）转变为自动处理（无意识、轻松、快速）。语言学习初期包含大量受控处理——查词、思考语法规则、翻译。要达到流利，就必须把这些知识转化为自动处理能力；而这种转化只有通过不进行有意识分析的反复、持续接触才能实现。"}},{"id":"segment-0019","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"The distinction between freeflow (meaning-focused, automatic processing) and interactive immersion (form-focused, controlled processing) reflects Nation's (2007) \"four strands\" framework, which argues that language learning requires a balance of meaning-focused activity and deliberate study — and that fluency develops specifically through high-volume processing of familiar material at natural speed.","zh":"自由流沉浸（注重意义、自动处理）与互动式沉浸（注重形式、受控处理）之间的区别，呼应了 Nation（2007）的“四条主线”框架。该框架认为，语言学习需要在注重意义的活动和有意识的学习之间取得平衡；而流利度尤其需要通过以自然速度大量处理熟悉材料来培养。"}},{"id":"segment-0020","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"The research on input flooding and implicit learning (Truscott, 2007) supports the power of massive exposure. Learners exposed to large amounts of language through natural processing develop implicit grammatical knowledge comparable to or exceeding that of learners receiving explicit grammar instruction, without the cognitive load of conscious analysis. This is why freeflow — consuming large amounts of content naturally — is where true fluency develops.","zh":"关于输入洪流和内隐学习的研究（Truscott，2007）证明了海量接触的强大作用。通过自然处理接触大量语言的学习者，能够形成与接受显性语法教学的学习者相当、甚至更强的内隐语法知识，同时无须承担有意识分析带来的认知负担。因此，真正的流利正是在自由流沉浸——自然吸收大量内容——的过程中形成的。"}}],"cards":[]}}]
